#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -Eeuo pipefail

usage(){
  printf 'Usage: %s <INSTANCE_ID> [OUTPUT_MD]\n' "$(basename "$0")" >&2
  exit 64
}

[[ $# -ge 1 && $# -le 2 ]] || usage
INSTANCE_ID="$1"
REGISTRY_ROOT="${CARSON_REGISTRY_ROOT:-$HOME/.carson_agent_instances}"
INDEX="$REGISTRY_ROOT/.registry/$INSTANCE_ID.env"
[[ -f "$INDEX" ]] || { printf 'ERROR=unknown instance: %s\n' "$INSTANCE_ID" >&2; exit 1; }

STATE_ROOT="$(
  bash -c 'source "$1"; printf "%s" "${CARSON_STATE_ROOT:-}"' _ "$INDEX"
)"
[[ -f "$STATE_ROOT/instance.env" ]] ||
  { printf 'ERROR=instance manifest missing\n' >&2; exit 1; }
[[ -f "$STATE_ROOT/active-session.env" ]] ||
  { printf 'ERROR=instance is not running; start it first\n' >&2; exit 1; }

read_value(){
  bash -c 'source "$1"; printf "%s" "${!2:-}"' _ "$1" "$2"
}

A_DIR="$(read_value "$STATE_ROOT/instance.env" CARSON_A_DIR)"
B_DIR="$(read_value "$STATE_ROOT/instance.env" CARSON_B_DIR)"
DOWNLOAD_DIR="$(read_value "$STATE_ROOT/instance.env" CARSON_DOWNLOAD_DIR)"
SOURCE_ROOT="$(read_value "$STATE_ROOT/instance.env" CARSON_SOURCE_ROOT)"
SESSION_ID="$(read_value "$STATE_ROOT/active-session.env" CARSON_SESSION_ID)"
TASK_PREFIX="$(read_value "$STATE_ROOT/active-session.env" CARSON_TASK_PREFIX)"

[[ -n "$A_DIR" && -n "$SESSION_ID" && -n "$TASK_PREFIX" ]] ||
  { printf 'ERROR=incomplete active instance routing state\n' >&2; exit 1; }

INGEST="$SOURCE_ROOT/bin/carson-ingest"
OUTPUT="${2:-$HOME/storage/shared/CARSON_LLM_BOOTSTRAP_${INSTANCE_ID}_${SESSION_ID}.md}"
mkdir -p "$(dirname "$OUTPUT")"

cat > "$OUTPUT" <<EOF
# CARSON arbitrary-LLM task bootstrap

This attachment is the complete routing contract for a local Termux agent
harness. Use it as authoritative context for tasks the user asks you to perform
through that harness.

## Active target

- Protocol: \`CARSON_DOWNLOAD_AGENT_V1\`
- Instance ID: \`$INSTANCE_ID\`
- Session ID: \`$SESSION_ID\`
- Required filename prefix: \`$TASK_PREFIX\`
- Stable result file on this device: \`$A_DIR/NEXT_LLM_MESSAGE.txt\`

Do not invent, shorten, replace, or reuse different instance/session values.
If a later bootstrap attachment supplies new routing values, the newer
attachment supersedes these values.

## What to emit when the user gives you a task

Create one genuinely downloadable executable shell artifact. Its filename must
begin exactly with:

\`$TASK_PREFIX\`

and end in \`.sh\`. Use a descriptive task name plus a unique suffix after the
prefix.

The file must begin with these routing lines exactly:

\`\`\`bash
#!/data/data/com.termux/files/usr/bin/bash
# CARSON_AGENT_PROTOCOL=CARSON_DOWNLOAD_AGENT_V1
# CARSON_INSTANCE_ID=$INSTANCE_ID
# CARSON_SESSION_ID=$SESSION_ID
# CARSON_PAYLOAD_TYPE=NEXT_LLM_TASK
\`\`\`

Then implement the user's requested Termux-side task. Use
\`set -Eeuo pipefail\` unless the task specifically requires different shell
semantics.

The payload's stdout becomes the next message returned through the harness, so
print concise structured results and a useful \`NEXT_LLM_INSTRUCTION\` at the
end. Errors should go to stderr and exit nonzero.

Do not put passwords, access tokens, private keys, or other secret values into
the downloadable task unless the user explicitly requires that exact handling.
Prefer reading secrets from already-existing local files or environment state.

## Response format

When you emit a task, give the user:

1. a short TL;DR;
2. the downloadable \`.sh\` attachment;
3. one Termux command that ingests the downloaded filename and waits for this
   exact task's result.

Because different AI clients may save attachments in different accessible
locations, do not assume the client saved the file directly into the harness
inbox. For a generated filename \`<ACTUAL_FILENAME>.sh\`, use this pattern:

\`\`\`bash
"$INGEST" "$INSTANCE_ID" "<ACTUAL_FILENAME>.sh"; timeout 120s sh -c 'until grep -Fq "SOURCE_FILE=<ACTUAL_FILENAME>.sh" "$A_DIR/NEXT_LLM_MESSAGE.txt" 2>/dev/null; do sleep 1; done'; cat "$A_DIR/NEXT_LLM_MESSAGE.txt"
\`\`\`

The ingest helper searches common Termux-accessible shared-storage download
locations by exact filename and copies the file into the configured harness
inbox when necessary. If an AI client stores its download in app-private
storage that Termux cannot access, the user must first save/share the attachment
into Termux-accessible shared storage or pass an accessible full path to the
ingest helper.

## Operating rule

Once a task result is pasted back into the chat, treat the text between
\`---BEGIN_NEXT_LLM_MESSAGE---\` and \`---END_NEXT_LLM_MESSAGE---\` as the next
harness-produced context and continue toward the user's objective. Emit the
next routed download file when another Termux-side step is required.
EOF

printf 'BOOTSTRAP_STATUS=PASS\n'
printf 'INSTANCE_ID=%s\n' "$INSTANCE_ID"
printf 'SESSION_ID=%s\n' "$SESSION_ID"
printf 'TASK_PREFIX=%s\n' "$TASK_PREFIX"
printf 'A_DIR=%s\n' "$A_DIR"
printf 'DOWNLOAD_DIR=%s\n' "$DOWNLOAD_DIR"
printf 'OUTPUT_MD=%s\n' "$OUTPUT"
